$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Mitsunobu Reaction
Using DPPBE Synthesis of 4-Phenethyloxy-benzoic Acid Methyl Ester (Table
1, entry 2): To a solution of 2-phenylethanol (1 mmol) in THF (3 mL) was
added successively methyl 4-hydroxy-benzoate (1.2 mmol) and DPPBE (1.3
mmol, 0.5 M/THF). A solution of DIAD (1.3 mmol) in THF (0.5 mL) was added
drop wise over 15 min at r.t. and the progress of the reaction was
monitored by TLC. Typically after 1 h tetrabutyl-ammonium fluoride in THF
(1 M, 2.5 mmol) was added. After 1 h at r.t. the reaction was
concentrated to dryness and the residue was taken-up in EtOAc, washed
with aq NaOH, H2O and brine, dried (MgSO4), filtered and evaporated to
dryness. The residue was purified by flash chromatography using
hexane-EtOAc (95:5) to give 4-phenethyloxy-benzoic acid methyl ester.
Table 1. Entry 6, yield 71%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mitsunobu reaction, optimization study of phosphine
reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Removable phosphine reagents for the Mitsunobu reaction
