$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the epoxide synthesis
(Scheme S-2) In a round-bottomed flask the desired diol and phosphine
were disolved in anhydrous CH2Cl2 at room temperature. Next, neat DIAD
was added dropwise (5-10 seconds) and the reaction progress was followed
by TLC. Once the reaction finished, the solvent was removed under vacuum
and the crude purified by column chromatography (on SiO2/NEt3 2.5%,
hexane as eluent).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mitsunobu cyclodeyhydration
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phosphine-Dependent Stereoselectivity in the Mitsunobu Cyclodehydration
of 1,2-Diols: Stereodivergent Approach to Triaryl-Substituted Epoxides
