$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Mitsunobu Reaction of amino alcohols with
2-bromophenol: The amino alcohol (1.0 equiv.) was dissolved in Benzene
(0.1M) with the 2- bromophenol (1.5 equiv.) and triphenylphosphine (1.5
equiv.). Solid 1,1'-Azodicarbonyldipiperidine (1.5 equiv.) was then added
and the reaction mixture stirred for 12h, then diluted with EtOAc and
washed with 1M NaOH (x 2) and brine (x 1). The EtOAc layer was then dried
over K2CO3 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue thus
obtained was chromatographed over SiO2 to yield the aminoether.
(1S,2S)-Dimethyl-[1-methyl-2-(2-bromophenoxy)-2-phenylethyl]-amine.
Colorless oil. Yield: 93%. Rf = 0.31 (TEA-washed SiO2, Hexanes/EtOAc/TEA
: 83:17:1).; (1R, 2R)-[2-(2-Bromophenoxy)-1-phenylpropyl]-dimethylamine.
Colorless oil. Yield: 5%. Rf = 0.38 (TEA-washed SiO2, Hexanes/EtOAc/TEA :
83:17:1).
(1S,2S)-Dimethyl-[1-methyl-2-(2-bromophenoxy)-2-phenylethyl]-amine. Rf =
0.31 IR (film/cm-1): 1475s, 1244s, 1030m, 746s, 702m. δH (500MHz, CDCl3):
0.94 (d, J7Hz, 3H, -CHCH3), 2.44 (s, 6H, -NCH3), 3.18 (q, J7Hz, 1H,
-NCHCH3), 5.23 (d, J7Hz, 1H, -OCHPh), 6.70 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 7.03 (dt, J8Hz,
1.5Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.29 (m, 5H, Ar-H), 7.47 (dd, 1H, J8Hz, 2Hz, 1H, Ar-H).
δc (125MHz, CDCl3): 12.7, 42.1, 63.9, 82.7, 112.8, 114.7, 121.6, 127.3,
127.8, 128.1, 128.4, 133.3, 139.1, 154.2.HRMS found 334.0811. C17H21BrNO
(MH+) requires 334.0806. [α]D (23°C) = -59.0 (c = 2.37, CHCl3). (1R,
2R)-[2-(2-Bromophenoxy)-1-phenylpropyl]-dimethylamine. Rf = 0.38 IR
(film/cm-1): 1475s, 1245s, 1030m, 748s, 704m. δH (500MHz, CDCl3): 1.13
(d, J6Hz, 3H, -CHCH3), 2.30 (s, 6H, -NCH3), 3.59 (d, J6.5Hz, 1H, -NCHPh),
4.90(dq, J6.5Hz, 6Hz, 1H, -OCHMe), 6.82 (dt, J8Hz, 1.5Hz 1H, Ar-H), 6.98
(d, J8.5Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.22-7.34 (m, 6H, Ar-H), 7.54 (dd, 1H, J8Hz, 2Hz,
1H, Ar- H). δc (125MHz, CDCl3): 16.4, 43.8, 74.1, 75.8, 113.9, 115.5,
122.1, 127.4, 128.0, 128.3, 129.7, 133.7, 137.7, 154.4. HRMS found
334.0806. C17H21BrNO (MH+) requires 334.0806. [α]D (23°C) = -17.5 (c =
0.28, CHCl3).
