$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Mitsunobu Reaction:
To a refluxing solution of 6-OH thiazolylpyrrolidine (150 mg, 0.30 mmol),
PPh3 (120 mg, 0.45 mmol), and phenol or carboxylic acid derivative (0.60
mmol) in anhyd THF (6 mL) was added DIAD (90 mL, 0.45 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred at 80 °C for 2 h and then concentrated. The residue
was eluted from a column of silica gel (cyclohexane-EtOAc) to give the
pyrrolidine 6 and the piperidine 7. Compound 9a : Yield 71 % ; Compound
10a : Yield 29 %. Compound 9a: [α ]D = -4.6 (c 0.6, CHCl3). Compound 10a:
[α ]D = +10.0 (c 0.7, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective, Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ring enlargement of polyhydroxylated pyrrolidines to piperidines by
Mitsunobu reaction: A fortuitous synthesis of 1-deoxy-L-allonojirimycin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
